          ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied). \n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}6 & 0 & 0 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}8 & 7 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{21}\\ne 0$ (condition  II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are in row echelon form."
        },
