          ":question/problem": "Which of the following augmented matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since ${b}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the first row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are **not** in row echelon form."
