              ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 11 & 10 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n",
              ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that by replacing $a_{32}$, $a_{42}$, and $a_{43}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A  &= \\begin{bmatrix}\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} & 11 & 10 & 9 \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{4} & 7 & 8 \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{red}-1}} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{6} & 5 \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{red}1}} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{red}2}} & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &\\longrightarrow \\begin{bmatrix}\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} & 11 & 10 & 9 \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{4} & 7 & 8 \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & {\\color{blue}0} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{6} & 5 \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & {\\color{blue}0} & {\\color{blue}0} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{4}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"
            },
